      "text_raw": "A more elaborate example is\nshown in this slide.\nAgain, linear amplifier are\nused at the inputs, which\nsaturate.\nResistors are connected\nbetween the outputs of the\namplifiers to create thresh-\nold voltages for the latches,\nwhich lie in between the ref-\nerence voltages 0 V, 0.25 V,\n0.5 V, 0.75 V and 1 V. Four\nresistors are inserted. As a\nresult, three out of four\namplifiers can be left out.\nThis results in consider-\nable savings in power consumption and especially input capacitance.\nThe actual operation is discussed next.",
      "text": "A more elaborate example is shown in this slide. Again, linear amplifier are used at the inputs, which saturate. Resistors are connected between the outputs of the amplifiers to create threshold voltages for the latches, which lie in between the reference voltages 0 V, 0.25 V, 0.5 V, 0.75 V and 1 V. Four resistors are inserted. As a result, three out of four amplifiers can be left out. This results in considerable savings in power consumption and especially input capacitance. The actual operation is discussed next."
